<Base title="Enterprise licensing and implementation" description="Explore scoped customer-hosted Smart Exam licensing, implementation, integration and support."><section class="page-hero"><div class="container page-title-only"><span class="eyebrow">Enterprise licensing</span><h1>Define the right scope before the price.</h1><p class="intro">Build a proposal around your examination workflows, customer-hosted deployment, implementation and support requirements.</p></div></section><section class="section-space"><div class="container"><div class="license-grid"><article class="license-card"><span class="eyebrow">Software and deployment</span><h2>A defined enterprise license.</h2><p>Discuss license duration, the agreed deployment, permitted use and the workflows your organization needs.</p><ul class="check-list"><li>Examination and candidate operations</li><li>Department and role model</li><li>Scoped proctoring and evidence workflows</li><li>Customer-hosted implementation</li></ul><a href="/request-quote/" class="button button-dark">Request a quote</a></article><article class="license-card"><span class="eyebrow">Delivery and operations</span><h2>A practical implementation plan.</h2><p>Agree the work, dependencies and acceptance required to make the deployment useful for your teams.</p><ul class="check-list"><li>Configuration and administrator training</li><li>Separately scoped integrations</li><li>Acceptance and recovery planning</li><li>Support responsibilities and hours</li></ul><a href="/request-demo/" class="button button-outline">Discuss your requirements</a></article></div><div class="long-copy"><h2>What shapes the proposal?</h2><p>Assessment volume and concurrent peak, session duration, departments, identity integration, recording scope and retention, installation requirements and support expectations. Capacity and service commitments follow validation of the proposed configuration.</p><h2>Plan the whole operating cost.</h2><p>Software, implementation and support are one part of the picture. Customer infrastructure, database licenses, storage, backups, media relays, external providers and internal operations may carry separate costs.</p><h2>License terms are agreed in writing.</h2><p>License duration, update rights, maintenance, renewal, permitted environments and exit arrangements belong in the final agreement. No fixed public price, managed SaaS offer or unlimited-use commitment is implied by this page.</p></div></div></section><CTA title="Build a proposal your teams can evaluate." href="/request-quote/" label="Request a quote" /></Base>
